# The build context is this directory, and the image must contain only the binary plus
# an example config and an example passwd file (§2.3). Everything the Go build does not
# read is excluded, so nothing can reach the image by accident.

.git
.DS_Store
*.log

# The test corpus. §2.3 bars it from the image; excluding it from the context as well
# keeps a fixture hostname out of every build layer (I2).
fixtures/

# The frontend source and its dependency tree. What the binary serves is the bundle
# committed under internal/webui/dist, embedded at compile time — the UI source is
# never needed to build the image, and §2.3 says no source may be in it.
web/

# Documentation, the deployment example, and the sidecar example. The image ships the
# config and passwd examples only.
*.md
compose.yml
.labview.example
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# An operator's real config, if they mounted one here.
config/
config.local.yml
